#usda 1.0
(
    """Reshape the YAM's chain into the one AUTOLab's GaP v1.0 plans on.

    Opt-in: the `kinematics` axis's default `i2rt` is the real robot (I2RT
    v1.2.4 onward, CAD-aligned), and this layer moves it away from that.

    AUTOLab's RoboSimStudio embodiment `yam_i2rt` (cable routing, USB-C) is
    composed from I2RT's interim yam.xml (2026-03 .. 2026-07, the AUTOLab pin
    i2rt@c40b4125), which I2RT replaced in v1.2.4. Its PyRoKi IK checks its
    URDF of that chain against the simulated arm at construction and refuses a
    tool-link-to-TCP drift over 1.0 mm between two poses, falling back to
    another solver. Against the default (`i2rt`) chain it measures 1.09 mm:

      | in the base frame at q = 0       | i2rt (default) | AUTOLab yam_i2rt |
      | shoulder (joint2) axis height    | 114.0 mm       | 112.5 mm         |
      | joint4 -> joint5 axis offset     |  74.0 mm       |  70.385 mm       |
      | wrist (joint5/6) lateral offset  |   0            |   3.589 mm       |
      | joint6 axis height - joint4's    |   0            |  -0.199 mm       |

    So a simulator standing in for AUTOLab's cell runs AUTOLab's solver only
    on AUTOLab's chain. This layer makes it so by moving two bodies, each with
    its whole subtree and its joint anchor:

    - link_2 down 1.5 mm along joint1's axis: the shoulder height;
    - link_5 by (-3.616, +3.589, -0.199) mm in the base frame at q = 0,
      (3.616, 0.199, -3.589) mm in link_4's frame: the wrist offsets.

    The two-pose drift against AUTOLab's yam_i2rt_arm.urdf is then under
    0.01 mm. Meshes ride on their bodies, so the joints between link_4 and
    link_5 and between link_1 and link_2 show a few-millimetre seam.
    """
)
over "i2rt_yam"
{
    over "Geometry"
    {
        over "arm"
        {
            over "link_1"
            {
                over "link_2"
                {
                    double3 xformOp:translate = (0.000025, -0.02, 0.0394)

                    over "joint2"
                    {
                        point3f physics:localPos0 = (0.000025, -0.02, 0.0394)
                    }

                    over "link_3"
                    {
                        over "link_4"
                        {
                            over "link_5"
                            {
                                double3 xformOp:translate = (-0.0703842, -0.0393005, -0.0035644)

                                over "joint5"
                                {
                                    point3f physics:localPos0 = (-0.0703842, -0.0393005, -0.0035644)
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
